                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "cd03391c-5213-40ad-aff3-d408a4039308",
                        "entry_id": "09bdb8f3-5a66-3058-8250-b77777571f71",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "transmecs"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e00c75b8-4f0b-3201-96bd-34c4f21cfcc9",
                        "entry_id": "09bdb8f3-5a66-3058-8250-b77777571f71",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Homme trans."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "familiar"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2c94f34-812e-41ba-be4c-6e093939ff44",
                                "sense_id": "e00c75b8-4f0b-3201-96bd-34c4f21cfcc9",
                                "text": "Je devrais enlever \"méchant transmec\" de ma bio parce-qu’en vrai j’suis pas si méchant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f04716f-736b-4155-a7af-4065ab63b4dc",
                                "sense_id": "e00c75b8-4f0b-3201-96bd-34c4f21cfcc9",
                                "text": "Non je ne suis pas LE transmec. Le beau mec, bien réussi, masculin, viril, hormoné, celui qui relationne avec des filles, des meufs, des fems, mais qui est super déconstruit."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c79a8cbc-c344-4246-b59d-9f87422428c9",
                        "source_entry_id": "09bdb8f3-5a66-3058-8250-b77777571f71",
                        "source_sense_id": "e00c75b8-4f0b-3201-96bd-34c4f21cfcc9",
                        "target_lang_word": "transguy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "transguy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                        "entry_id": "313abc05-ef5f-3a33-bc64-a4dc74691e3c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of trans guy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed71a440-0f7c-489b-bb66-a9a979794e16",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "Queer couple, straight privilege! I think of him as a transguy-in my mind, a step above ordinary guys. For me, that's the absolute ideal, the best of both worlds."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37159a8b-ee05-4561-919a-1574c67e0241",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "ViolyntFemme is a twenty-seven-year-old High Femme married to the Transguy of her dreams."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff6ec028-ba2d-4f0b-90c0-ebbe407324bf",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "Once I was introduced to a transguy at a sex party, and the very first thing he did was complain bitterly to me about how a lesbian had just hit on him, mistaking him for a dyke."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af4156f0-1653-4b2d-bbe3-91093f0333a7",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "It was like I had to grow up all over again and learn how to live as a new person, as a transguy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df270706-4e8b-4aeb-8fb3-f1decbbc7efb",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "Although I received a sufficient amount of responses from white people with a working-class background or limited economic resources, and my sample includes people between 20 and 60 years of age, people of color are underrepresented in my sample, which might also have to do with the fact that I'm white myself and that the more formal BDSM communities are dominated by white people, as the white, queer transguy Matt suggests in regard to the local women/trans and queer play parties."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da2de955-3ee6-4941-b04e-8a952e021e29",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "Myself, El, and Jacob, a shy gay transguy who also hangs out with us after the workshop, sit in Costa Coffee and proceed do what seems to happen every time I meet new transpeople."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0029875-4b16-4bfa-9aee-18206b9b9a32",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "I just don't introduce myself as “Hi, I'm Craig the transguy.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fbeb8092-5761-4970-8c9e-bb34e053a98b",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "Some FTMs feel disrespected when someone whose main commitment to gender change has been the purchase of a few neckties starts calling himself a transguy, as though their entire gender could really be summed up that way."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0254fc31-8518-4a1f-aaea-e7247f19b42f",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "Teiresias went on to narrate coming out as queer and, later, as a transguy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6884a470-31ff-4bd3-b105-414953650443",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "For instance, a transman/transguy is usually someone who was labeled female at birth but now identifies as a man or a male."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50a50636-8db3-4cb7-b359-99cb53c80dbc",
                                                "sense_id": "6143ca23-425d-36a6-a449-532cda63530c",
                                                "text": "I'm a transguy who can't wait to physically transition."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "db84ea9f-5061-4540-8905-e3887f617788",
                        "source_entry_id": "09bdb8f3-5a66-3058-8250-b77777571f71",
